<title>SPAIN: Spain's Telefonica H1 net up 19.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Telefonica H1 net up 19.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for Telefonica group six months to June in billions of pesetas, unless stated:</p>
<p>					   H1 1996	    H1 1995</p>
<p> Net attrib. profit		  71.887     vs    60.147</p>
<p> Operating income		   954.929     vs   852.546</p>
<p> Operating profit		   256.568     vs   245.488</p>
<p> Operating costs		     493.553    vs    407.400</p>
<p> Extraordinary profit		-45.896    vs    -37.173</p>
<p> Pretax profit			 124.933    vs    106.229</p>
<p> Earnings per share (ptas)	  76.52     vs     64.02</p>
<p> Cash flow per share (ptas)	412.52     vs    390.22</p>
<p> Breakdown of business by division</p>
<p> Basic telephony		     675.347     vs   599.573</p>
<p> Mobile telephony		    110.182     vs    49.343</p>
<p> International service	     163.252     vs   143.848</p>
<p>- NOTE: Telefonica said the improvement in results was due to income growth, including a rise in revenues from new basic telephony services. Continued strong growth of mobile telephony and the international service also helped, the firm said.</p>
<p>Personnel cost growth slowed significantly. Financial charges also fell 19.3 percent, helped by a decrease in debt and falling interest rates.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
